# JellyfinCollectionsPlugin repo layout

Root: `D:\Banaat\JellyfinCollectionsPlugin\` — all project files stay here, not on `C:\`.

## Top-level folders

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `src/Jellyfin.Plugin.Collections/` | Jellyfin server-side plugin (C#) |
| `src/Jellyfin.Plugin.Collections.Tests/` | xUnit tests |
| `.github/workflows/` | CI and release (used only if/when the repo is published) |
| `build.yaml`, `manifest.json` (repo root) | Plugin packaging (jprm metadata, plugin repository manifest) |
| `scripts/` | Build, package, and maintenance scripts |
| `docs/` | Design notes, intent, and user documentation |
| `Chats/` | Cursor chat/session data — gitignored |
| `github/` | Local push/pull backup scripts |

## General rules

- Project-specific artifacts belong in the matching repo subfolder (nested subfolders preferred).
- Generic Cursor/tooling files not tied to this project → `D:\Apps\Cursor\` with appropriate subfolders.
- Never commit secrets, chat archives, or local build output (`bin/`, `obj/`).
- Local `D:\Banaat\` is source of truth; GitHub is backup only (see `github-backup-local-source-of-truth.mdc`).
